    "print(\"Fast-output routes disconnected.\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "signal-dc-setup-note",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 8. Test 1: configure the DC source\n",
    "\n",
    "PID0 drives OUT1 with P=I=0 and adjustable integrator memory. PID1 reads IN1 without driving an output; this is the same DC-source arrangement used on Gen 1."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "signal-dc-setup",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "src = rp.pid0\n",
    "src.output_direct = \"off\"\n",
    "src.input = \"in1\"\n",
    "src.p = 0\n",
    "src.i = 0\n",
    "src.setpoint = 0\n",
    "src.ival = 0\n",
    "src.min_voltage = -0.99\n",
    "src.max_voltage = 0.99\n",
    "src.inputfilter = [0, 0, 0]\n",
    "src.use_setpoint_sequence = False\n",
    "src.paused = False\n",
    "\n",
    "mon = rp.pid1\n",
    "mon.input = \"in1\"\n",
    "mon.output_direct = \"off\"\n",
    "mon.p = 1\n",
    "mon.i = 0\n",
    "mon.setpoint = 0\n",
    "mon.ival = 0\n",
    "mon.min_voltage = -0.99\n",
    "mon.max_voltage = 0.99\n",
    "mon.inputfilter = [0, 0, 0]\n",
    "mon.use_setpoint_sequence = False\n",
    "mon.paused = False\n",
    "src.output_direct = \"out1\""
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "signal-dc-measure-note",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 9. Measure the five DC levels\n",
    "\n",
    "At each of the same five commands, read the Rigol DC voltage and enter it in volts. The table preserves both RP readbacks and the physical measurement; do not enter the old Gen 1 values. On completion or interruption, the DC output is disconnected."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "signal-dc-measure",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "DC_COMMANDS = [-0.5, -0.25, 0.0, 0.25, 0.5]\n",
    "dc_rows = []\n",
    "src.output_direct = \"out1\"\n",
    "try:\n",
    "    for command in DC_COMMANDS:\n",
    "        src.ival = command\n",
    "        time.sleep(0.3)\n",
    "        rigol_volts = float(input(f\"Command {command:+.2f}: Rigol DC voltage [V]: \"))\n",
    "        if not np.isfinite(rigol_volts):\n",
    "            raise ValueError(\"Enter a finite measured voltage.\")\n",
    "        row = {\n",
    "            \"command\": command,\n",
    "            \"rp_output\": float(src.current_output_signal),\n",
    "            \"rp_in1\": float(rp.scope.voltage_in1),\n",
    "            \"rp_pid1\": float(mon.current_output_signal),\n",
    "            \"rigol_volts\": rigol_volts,\n",
    "        }\n",
    "        dc_rows.append(row)\n",
    "        print(json.dumps(row))\n",
    "finally:\n",
    "    src.ival = 0\n",
    "    src.output_direct = \"off\"\n",
    "print(json.dumps(dc_rows, indent=2))"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "signal-dc-fit-note",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 10. Fit this board's output and input separately\n",
    "\n",
    "Calculate volts = gain × RP readback + offset for OUT1 and IN1, with RMS residuals. These are notebook-only conversions; no driver calibration changes. The PID setpoint uses the IN1 fit, not the output fit."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "signal-dc-fit",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "def fit_dc_calibration(rows):\n",
    "    data = np.asarray([[r[\"rp_output\"], r[\"rp_in1\"], r[\"rigol_volts\"]]\n",
    "                       for r in rows], dtype=float)\n",
    "    if data.ndim != 2 or data.shape[0] < 3 or data.shape[1] != 3:\n",
    "        raise ValueError(\"At least three paired DC measurements are needed.\")\n",
    "    if not np.isfinite(data).all():\n",
    "        raise ValueError(\"DC measurements must be finite.\")\n",
    "    fits = []\n",
    "    for column in (0, 1):\n",
    "        x, y = data[:, column], data[:, 2]\n",
    "        if np.ptp(x) == 0:\n",
    "            raise ValueError(\"Readback did not change across DC levels; inspect wiring/range.\")\n",
    "        gain, offset = np.polyfit(x, y, 1)\n",
    "        if np.isclose(gain, 0):\n",
    "            raise ValueError(\"Measured gain is zero; inspect measurements before inversion.\")\n",
    "        rms = float(np.sqrt(np.mean((y - (gain * x + offset)) ** 2)))\n",
    "        fits.append((float(gain), float(offset), rms))\n",
    "    return fits\n",
    "\n",
    "out_fit, in_fit = fit_dc_calibration(dc_rows)\n",
    "RP_OUT_TO_RIGOL_GAIN, RP_OUT_TO_RIGOL_OFFSET, out_rms = out_fit\n",
    "RP_IN1_TO_RIGOL_GAIN, RP_IN1_TO_RIGOL_OFFSET, in_rms = in_fit\n",
    "\n",
    "def rp_to_rigol(value):\n",
    "    return RP_OUT_TO_RIGOL_GAIN * value + RP_OUT_TO_RIGOL_OFFSET\n",
    "\n",
    "def rigol_to_rp(value):\n",
    "    return (value - RP_OUT_TO_RIGOL_OFFSET) / RP_OUT_TO_RIGOL_GAIN\n",
    "\n",
    "def rp_in1_to_rigol(value):\n",
    "    return RP_IN1_TO_RIGOL_GAIN * value + RP_IN1_TO_RIGOL_OFFSET\n",
    "\n",
    "def rigol_to_rp_in1(value):\n",
    "    return (value - RP_IN1_TO_RIGOL_OFFSET) / RP_IN1_TO_RIGOL_GAIN\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"OUT1 fit (gain, offset V, RMS V):\", out_fit)\n",
    "print(\"IN1  fit (gain, offset V, RMS V):\", in_fit)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "signal-triangle-note",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 11. Test 2a: 1 Hz triangle\n",
    "\n",
    "The user confirmed both 1 Hz and 1 kHz worked on Gen 1. Start with its saved 1 Hz / amplitude 0.4 setting, then repeat at 1 kHz in step 13b. PID0 is disconnected; ASG0 drives OUT1. Record Rigol frequency, minimum, maximum, Vpp and RMS."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "signal-triangle",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "rp.pid0.output_direct = \"off\"\n",
    "asg = rp.asg0\n",
    "asg.output_direct = \"off\"\n",
    "asg.waveform = \"ramp\"\n",
    "asg.frequency = 1.0  # Hz, matching the saved Gen 1 code.\n",
    "asg.amplitude = 0.4\n",
    "asg.offset = 0.0\n",
    "asg.trigger_source = \"immediately\"\n",
    "asg.output_direct = \"out1\"\n",
    "print(\"ASG frequency [Hz]:\", asg.frequency)\n",
    "print(\"ASG amplitude [RP units]:\", asg.amplitude)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "signal-poll-note",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 12. Record the input trace\n",
    "\n",
    "Collect the same 5,000 software-polled IN1 readings. Record elapsed time as well: sleep plus SSH overhead is not a uniform sample interval. Compare amplitude/offset with the Rigol; the polled mean alone is not a DC calibration."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "signal-poll",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "vals, sample_times = [], []\n",
    "start = time.perf_counter()\n",
    "for _ in range(5000):\n",
    "    vals.append(rp.scope.voltage_in1)\n",
    "    sample_times.append(time.perf_counter() - start)\n",
    "    time.sleep(0.0005)\n",
    "vals = np.asarray(vals)\n",
    "sample_times = np.asarray(sample_times)\n",
    "print(\"RP mean =\", np.mean(vals))\n",
    "print(\"RP min =\", np.min(vals))\n",
    "print(\"RP max =\", np.max(vals))\n",
    "print(\"RP Vpp =\", np.ptp(vals))\n",
    "print(\"Elapsed [s] =\", sample_times[-1])"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "signal-plot-note",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 13. Plot and note the external measurement\n",
    "\n",
    "Plot the captured triangle against actual read times. Enter the Rigol observations below the plot so the local notebook retains the external evidence too."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "signal-plot",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "fig, ax = plt.subplots()\n",
    "ax.plot(sample_times, vals)\n",
    "ax.set(xlabel=\"Elapsed [s]\", ylabel=\"IN1 [PyRPL units]\")\n",
    "plt.show()\n",
    "triangle_observation = input(\"Rigol frequency / Min / Max / Vpp / RMS and observations: \")\n",
    "print(\"Triangle observation:\", triangle_observation)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "signal-fast-triangle-note",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 13b. Test 2b: 1 kHz triangle\n",
    "\n",
    "Repeat the same amplitude at 1 kHz. Use hardware-buffered RP scope acquisition plus the Rigol, not the slow polled trace above. After recording the observation, this cell restores 1 Hz for the saved Gen 1 PID-disturbance condition."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "id": "signal-fast-triangle",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "asg.frequency = 1000.0  # Hz\n",
    "try:\n",
    "    print(\"ASG frequency [Hz]:\", asg.frequency)\n",
    "    fast_times, fast_data = capture_scope(\"in1\", \"asg0\", duration=0.01)\n",
    "    fast_triangle_observation = input(\"Rigol 1 kHz frequency / Min / Max / Vpp / RMS and observations: \")\n",
    "    print(\"1 kHz triangle observation:\", fast_triangle_observation)\n",
    "finally:\n",
    "    asg.frequency = 1.0  # Restore the saved Gen 1 PID disturbance setting."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "signal-pid-note",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 14. Test 3: negative-I feedback with the ASG disturbance\n",
    "\n",
    "Repeat P=0, I=-150000 and a 0.5 V target using this board's IN1 calibration. As in the saved Gen 1 run, ASG0 stays routed to OUT1, summing its triangle with PID0 as a disturbance. The printed corrected setpoint is a calculation, not the measured output."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "signal-pid",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "pid = rp.pid0\n",
    "pid.output_direct = \"off\"\n",
    "pid.input = \"in1\"\n",
    "pid.min_voltage, pid.max_voltage = -1, 1\n",
    "pid.pause_gains = \"pi\"\n",
    "pid.paused = False\n",
    "pid.use_setpoint_sequence = False\n",
    "pid.p = 0\n",
    "pid.i = -150000\n",
    "pid.ival = 0\n",
    "desired_scope_voltage = 0.5\n",
    "pid.setpoint = rigol_to_rp_in1(desired_scope_voltage)\n",
    "pid.output_direct = \"out1\"\n",
    "print(\"raw RP setpoint =\", pid.setpoint)\n",
    "print(\"scope-corrected setpoint =\", rp_in1_to_rigol(pid.setpoint))\n",
    "print(\"ASG disturbance route:\", asg.output_direct)"
   ]
  },
  {
